WEBVTT

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.300
Did they find anything out of ordinary during your neurological exam?

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.040
Nope!

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.330
That's a relief then.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:52.570
Thank your parents for giving you such a sturdy body.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.510
I-I am thankful.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.010
However...

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.890
This is still an issue!

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.610
Be sure to change the compresses on your hips and left leg frequently.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.490
Also, you're not allowed to train at all for a while!

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.280
Y-You're kidding!

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.900
Not even light training?

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.950
Okay. I won't do any training.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.330
Here, I want you to use this.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.670
A-Aren't we getting carried away?

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.160
I can still walk-

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:28.670
O-Okay. I'll use it.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.490
Now, Ippo-kun,

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.010
let me make myself perfectly clear.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:40.510
You should no longer rely on the Dempsey Roll!

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.600
The old version puts too much stress on your body already.{move-version}

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:52.670
But that new stop-and-go action is shortening your career as we speak.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:58.240
Using that move will only hasten your retirement.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.150
<i>Retirement?</i>

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.770
You still haven't reached your goal, have you?

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.710
Do you want everything to end here?

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.710
If you want to reach your goal,

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.300
do not use that move.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.730
I know you have the ability to keep winning without it.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.220
<i>Win without the Dempsey Roll?</i>

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:32.430
<i>But... could I have knocked Sawamura-san out cold without using it?</i>

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.830
<i>If I'm going to continue facing boxers as good as him...</i>

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.150
<i>How am I supposed to win?</i>

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.470
<i>You still haven't reached your goal, have you?</i>

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.350
<i>Do you want everything to end here?</i>

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.750
<i>If you want to reach your goal...</i>

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.860
<i>I know I'm almost there.</i>

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.110
<i>I can't hold myself back.</i>

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:57.260
<i>I don't care what happens to me.</i>

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.260
<i>If I don't reach him, all is lost.</i>

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:10.940
Umezawa-kun!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.660
Say, Ippo.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:24.620
Do you remember the promise I made back when I started working for Makunouchi Fishing Boat?

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:25.740
Promise?

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.830
Oh, yeah! Of course!

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:30.080
<i>P-Please look!</i>

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.270
<i>This is good!</i>

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.090
<i>Did you draw this, Umezawa-kun?!</i>

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:46.050
<i>I never knew you had this talent!</i>

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.040
<i>Oh, is this your dream?{changed "was" to "is"}</i>

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.700
<i>Y-Yeah, it is. I want to become a mangaka.</i>

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.770
<i>Once I'm done, you'll be the first to see it!</i>

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:59.820
<i>I'll make you say it's totally awesome!</i>

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:03.410
So that means you're done with your manga?!

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:07.580
Yeah, and I was thinking of entering it in an amateur manga contest.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.840
Oh my gosh! I want to read it!

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.150
Please do. I'm proud of it.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.900
I can't wait!

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.170
Also, Ippo.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:26.800
I already told the boss this, but I'm gonna quit Makunouchi Fishing Boat.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:32.550
I made up my mind when I saw you face Sawamura.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.110
I want to chase my dream of becoming a mangaka.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.960
I'm a man, too.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.390
I don't want to lose.

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:47.070
I don't know if they'll come true, but I still have dreams!

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.990
I want to draw manga!

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.830
This is my debut match!

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.330
You have to do it, Umezawa-kun!

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.340
Ippo...

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.390
Wow! So many pages!

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:12.090
Now you're making me nervous!

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.350
Go on, read already!

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.350
It's a fishing manga!

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.670
I wanted to make it about boxing.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:23.670
But I plan to do it in a serial after I improve my art.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.360
And I already got my story material from working here.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:27.860
Sure!

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.380
Hello, Senpai!

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.870
Huh, if it isn't Itagaki-kun.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.830
I'm not a great reviewer,

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:39.380
so I thought having someone who could give an objective criticism would be a good idea.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.920
Y-You did?

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:44.080
Having another reader makes me twice as nervous.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:45.260
But, sure, go ahe-

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.550
Hey!

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:50.800
Wh-What? G-Guys?!

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.410
I hope this is a good manga.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.700
I know manga like the back of my hand.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:01.190
Hell, my name begins with the same letter as "manga"!

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:05.400
Y-You're kidding! Are you fine gentlemen going to read it too?{gentleman - gentlemen}

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.810
Wh-Why'd you bring them here?

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:10.530
Why not? It's better to have more readers.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.080
Let me have it.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.700
Uh, sure...

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.250
If it doesn't make me laugh, I'm wringing your neck.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.430
Are there funny scenes?

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:23.710
Help me! This isn't a gag manga!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.710
We each read a page at a time!

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:29.220
Hey, hold on a sec!

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:31.470
Oh, it's a fishing manga.

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:32.800
What kind of hook is that?

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.810
Who the hell gets hooked after one frickin' page?

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.040
What's that, you shithead?!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:37.830
<i>Aww...</i>

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.810
<i>I'm a dead man walking.</i>

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.820
Ooh! It looks like he got a huge one!

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.410
Gimme the next page!

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:47.990
Hold your horses! This is getting good!

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.230
That's a good sign, right?

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:50.860
Yeah...

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.910
Hand it over, asswipe!

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.080
Give me some goddamn time to read!

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:56.510
Leggo!

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:56.950
No way!

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.210
I wanna keep reading, assclown!

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:03.530
Wh-What have you done?

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:07.210
Umezawa-kun poured his heart and soul into that draft!

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:10.300
How are you going to fix this?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.720
They're getting away!

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.850
Mend what you destroyed!

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:22.690
Why did you even come here?! You scumbags!

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.020
<i>Umezawa-kun!</i>

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.410
I-I'm sorry!

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:40.000
If I hadn't called Itagaki-kun!

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.070
It's my fault!

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:42.970
I'll help you redraw the draft!

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:52.680
G-Get yourself together, Umezawa-kun.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.680
Did you hear that, Ippo?

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:57.980
"I wanna keep reading."

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:00.070
"Give me time to read."

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:03.690
And did you see them fighting over my draft?

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:04.950
Yeah.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.650
I sure did.

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:10.240
All right! I'm gonna redo the draft and submit it immediately!

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.150
I'm gonna do this!

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:13.780
Umezawa-kun.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:17.180
I wasn't really as confident as I let on.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:20.420
I was really worried they would pan it.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.540
Everybody gets worried!

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.920
Anyway, take that first step forward, Umezawa-kun!

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:28.710
Yeah, I know I will!

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.930
Argh! I went outside the line!

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:37.430
Relax, here's some whiteout.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:41.390
They only ripped three pages. This will only take us a night.

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:44.940
I should be sorry for having the national champ help me out.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:46.750
<i>A whole night?</i>

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.940
<i>For just three pages?</i>

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:56.340
<i>So he spent several nights making that draft, 
then coming to work first thing in the morning?</i>

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:00.990
<i>He's been working for us ever since Mom's hospitalization,</i>

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:03.500
<i>which greatly reduced her workload.</i>

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:07.540
<i>He's always there rooting for me before my matches.</i>

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.290
<i>We'll never know how much he helped Mom,</i>

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:13.140
<i>or how much he's supported me.</i>

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.550
I hope this manga sells.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.360
What are you saying? Don't jump the gun!

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.560
I haven't even submitted it yet!

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.790
I still got a long road ahead.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.260
<i>Thank you, Umezawa-kun!</i>

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.130
Go ahead, eat up!

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:51.550
I put all my culinary skills into this!

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:55.090
Don't be a stranger and come visit!

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:57.130
Sure.

00:09:57.130 --> 00:10:02.400
<i>I think I've gotten completely used to this easy pace and atmosphere.</i>

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.990
Sorry, Ippo.

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:07.470
You and your mom will have to do all the work around here.

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:10.100
That's what I'm really worried about.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.390
You don't have to worry about us!

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:12.870
Nope.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:15.530
You got your own dream of becoming a mangaka.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:24.620
What's wrong?

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:30.650
Th-There's something I really need to say before I go.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:33.250
Does it require you to be so formal?

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.510
It's something I have to do.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:44.640
Back in school, Ippo must've come home a lot of times covered in bruises.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:47.180
You probably already knew this, ma'am,

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:51.720
but it was because of bullies who said he smelled like worms.{smells-smelled}

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:55.610
About those bullies, the truth is...

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:57.450
That's enough, Umezawa-kun!

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.200
Look at me, Umezawa-kun.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:17.680
A man who is about to journey to a new world shouldn't hang his head down.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:21.350
You must always lift your head up and face forward.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:24.890
Good luck!

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:31.980
Thank you very much...

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.900
Thank you very much!

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:01.620
<i>It's hopeless.</i>

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:04.040
<i>I can't lift my head up.</i>

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.640
Umezawa-kun!

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:17.110
Umezawa-kun!

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:18.830
<i>Ippo?</i>

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:22.700
Your manga was really good!

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.700
What was that? I can't hear you!

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:29.700
Umezawa-kun! Your manga was really good!

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:38.110
Just like you are my very first fan,
 I'll be your very first fan!

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:46.050
That way we will, always and forever, be best friends!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:57.020
Yeah! Ippo!

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:59.020
Ippo!

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:10.180
Hi, guys!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.540
Good fighting out there!

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:13.040
Are you healing up?

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:16.200
That match moved me to tears!

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.670
Gee... thanks.

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:20.940
You sure you're all right, Ippo?

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.680
You're on a crutch like a damn cripple.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:26.050
You need to retire, Gimp Boy!

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:28.290
Don't you dare call me "Gimp Boy"!

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:31.120
I had to spend the whole night fixing that manga!

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.060
Ooh! Watch out, he's mad!

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.060
<i>He's not sorry at all!</i>

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:38.960
Hey, just ignore King Preposterous here.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.070
The two of us are sorry for what happened.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:46.330
If his manga's a hit, I'll send him a bouquet or something.

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:50.160
I'll invite him to an all-you-can-eat dinner at my restaurant.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:52.200
Kimura-san, Aoki-san...

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:54.190
I hope he makes it...

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:55.720
Me too...

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:57.570
My, aren't we all peachy keen?

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:00.930
Don't think I forgot about Umekou or nothing!

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:04.050
I spent all night making it.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:05.050
Based on actual events!

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:07.590
"The Road to the World Championship"!

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:12.790
Nobody asked you to do that!

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.210
What the hell are you thinking?!

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:15.370
I'm ripping it up!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:17.230
What are you pricks doing?!

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:24.310
Forgive my lateness. I wish to thank you for your help.

00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:25.190
Right.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:29.780
Let's cut to the chase and discuss your next match.

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:32.280
M-My next match?

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.480
Oh, this? Dr. Yamaguchi practically forced me to use it.{this - it}

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.200
She may be going overboard with the crutch,

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.760
but I can still do light exercises, no problem!

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.250
I'm heading over to train.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:45.420
You dimwit!

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:49.660
Listen to your doctor!

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:52.430
You need to focus on recuperation!

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:56.430
B-But we had to talk about my next match...

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.680
Remember these?

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:03.230
<i>Those are the challenges I received before the Sawamura fight.</i>

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:08.340
You must have really spooked them. They all withdrew their challenges.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:11.990
If nobody's gonna fight you,
 then there are no more title defenses.

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:13.990
Th-They withdrew?

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:18.000
I said you were a cheese champion before the Sawamura fight.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:24.870
But I guess your performance did away with any stray notions that you were full of holes.

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:28.870
Don't get conceited!

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.840
You're still not good enough as far as I'm concerned!

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:33.060
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:36.500
Where we go from now is still an unsettled matter.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:42.810
But rest up your body and build it up for that eventual match like the pro you are!

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.710
Yes, sir! Thank you very much!

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:55.140
That eventual match, you say?

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:59.080
If nobody in the country will fight him, then that means...

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:01.870
He'll need to rise up.

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:09.830
<i>Recuperation, huh?</i>

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.290
<i>But I guess he's...</i>

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:14.260
<i>My hips still hurt.</i>

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:20.640
<i>I had also been on edge nonstop before my match with Sawamura-san.</i>

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:26.350
<i>I suppose I need to give both my mind and body a rest.</i>

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:36.180
Welcome back, Senpai!

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:37.880
I-Itagaki-kun?

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:38.870
And Nanako-chan?

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.200
What's going on here?

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:42.720
We got some help.

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:45.250
They're filling in for Umezawa-kun.

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:48.060
What? You're going to work for us?

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:51.500
They just showed up out of the blue, but I'm so glad!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:56.010
B-But I didn't even put up "Help Wanted" posters.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.170
Umezawa-san gave me a call.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:02.050
He told me to take care of Makunouchi Fishing Boat.

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:03.640
He said that?

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:06.590
<i>Umezawa-kun...</i>

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:09.400
<i>He even thought about who to get to replace him.</i>

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:11.870
This is what I've dreamed of!

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:14.900
What other workplace can accommodate a boxer like me?

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:17.410
We're also a poor family who can really use the money.

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:19.750
Thanks for helping us, Itagaki-kun!

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:22.410
I look forward to working here.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:25.800
But I'm not sure we can take on two workers.

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:29.670
Don't worry about me. I'm just here to visit.

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:33.170
We wish to show our gratitude 
for the opportunity to work here.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:35.080
You Ita-got our thanks.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:43.350
Itagaki-kun, spread the bait!

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:44.680
Sure thing!

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:49.040
<i>Talk about unsteady.</i>

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:52.000
<i>But I must learn to balance myself firmly.</i>

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:56.480
<i>This must be the secret behind Senpai landing heavy blows while off-balance.</i>

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.520
<i>It must be.</i>

00:18:06.470 --> 00:18:09.240
<i>These are way heavier with fish in them.</i>

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:12.590
<i>Senpai's been doing this work for over ten years.</i>

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:19.050
<i>That's why he's so strong despite his lack of athletic experience.</i>

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.390
<i>I get it.</i>

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.760
<i>I get it...</i>

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.220
<i>I get it!</i>

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:34.150
Huh, Senpai?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.900
Have you healed up?

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:40.540
I've got some rest, thanks to you.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.450
Today I'm returning to work.

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:46.960
H-He lifted twice my load...

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:48.980
like it was nothing?

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:57.140
<i>I thought I'd catch up to him by living the same life as he does.</i>

00:18:57.140 --> 00:18:59.640
<i>But I'm still no match for Senpai.</i>

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:05.630
<i>However, I will still try to overtake him!</i>

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:13.590
Itagaki Manabu has been on fire all night!

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:16.480
What kind of action will we see in this second round?

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:39.520
Holy buckets, it's over!

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:43.390
He absolutely killed him with that off-balanced uppercut!

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:48.160
Don't you think he's gotten more built ever since he started working at Makunouchi's?

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:51.140
Spill it, Ippo! What's the secret?

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:53.810
Lemme work at Makunouchi Fishing Boat too!

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:55.420
Oh, no...

00:19:57.970 --> 00:19:59.510
Yeah!
